1
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:39,039
Who is she?

2
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:39,400
Qianjin.

3
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:39,840
Who?

4
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,199
You can't... No...

5
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:41,120
I asked you who she is!

6
00:02:41,479 --> 00:02:41,840
You can't...

7
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,520
Who is she?

8
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,120
Who is she?

9
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,080
Qianjin, Qianjin!

10
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,479
Qianjin, listen. Let me explain.

11
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:46,560
Why is she hitting you?

12
00:02:46,599 --> 00:02:47,800
You bastard!

13
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:50,120
What?

14
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:51,879
What are you doing?

15
00:02:51,879 --> 00:02:52,639
Stop it!

16
00:02:52,639 --> 00:02:53,680
Jiaqi, stop! Qianjin!

17
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:54,479
Stop it!

18
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:55,360
Wait, Jiaqi!

19
00:02:55,439 --> 00:02:56,039
Don't grab me!

20
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:57,120
What are you doing?

21
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:57,759
Let go! Let go!

22
00:02:57,759 --> 00:02:58,639
Stop hitting! Stop!

23
00:02:59,360 --> 00:02:59,800
Qianjin!

24
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:00,840
Stop fighting!

25
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:11,400
Jiaqi!

26
00:03:14,199 --> 00:03:15,199
She's my wife.

27
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,039
She's my daughter.

28
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,840
Since when do you have a daughter this old?

29
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,000
Do you want me to say something?

30
00:03:34,599 --> 00:03:35,280
Fine, I'll speak now.

31
00:03:37,039 --> 00:03:38,520
My name is Zhao Jiaqi.

32
00:03:38,599 --> 00:03:39,080
I'm 14 years old.

33
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,199
Shut up!

34
00:03:40,319 --> 00:03:40,960
Go ahead.

35
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,240
Shut up!

36
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:42,800
Shut up!

37
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,120
Why are you telling me to shut up?

38
00:03:44,319 --> 00:03:46,000
Why are you telling me to shut up?

39
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,080
Calm down. Just calm down.

40
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:47,639
Okay?

41
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:57,520
Qianjin.

42
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,919
Her mom and I were college classmates.

43
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,199
We dated in college.

44
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,879
Going abroad was all the rage back then, right?

45
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,319
So she insisted on leaving the country.

46
00:04:07,599 --> 00:04:09,039
Just as the paperwork was almost done,

47
00:04:09,919 --> 00:04:10,759
we found out

48
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,000
she was already pregnant.

49
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,560
I told her since she was pregnant,

50
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:15,520
she shouldn't go abroad.

51
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:16,439
Stay here,

52
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:17,920
and let's get married, right?

53
00:04:19,879 --> 00:04:20,279
Qianjin.

54
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:21,199
Qianjin! Qianjin!

55
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,360
Let go of me!

56
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:22,839
You can't leave!

57
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:23,959
Qianjin, let me explain, please?

58
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,519
Just let me finish, Qianjin!

59
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:26,560
Where are you going?

60
00:04:26,759 --> 00:04:27,480
To see my dad!

61
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:28,000
You can't go to Dad!

62
00:04:28,399 --> 00:04:29,360
You really can't go to Dad right now!

63
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,120
Just wait till my dad deals with you!

64
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:31,519
Qianjin!

65
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:32,480
Qianjin!

66
00:04:33,399 --> 00:04:34,160
Dad has cancer!

67
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,480
What did you say?

68
00:04:41,759 --> 00:04:42,600
Prostate cancer.

69
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:45,319
Late-stage.

70
00:05:13,199 --> 00:05:14,120
I told her back then

71
00:05:14,879 --> 00:05:15,720
to have the baby,

72
00:05:17,759 --> 00:05:18,759
but she refused.

73
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:21,240
She said having a kid

74
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:22,439
would keep her from going abroad.

75
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,759
I never expected that

76
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:25,680
the moment her visa was approved,

77
00:05:26,839 --> 00:05:27,839
she would leave just a few days later.

78
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,240
Before you and I got married,

79
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,480
she came back once.

80
00:05:34,839 --> 00:05:36,199
She said after arriving in the US,

81
00:05:37,319 --> 00:05:37,839
she couldn't bear to do it,

82
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:39,920
so she had the baby.

83
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:41,879
She also told me

84
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,800
she could raise her on her own

85
00:05:43,959 --> 00:05:44,639
without any help from me.

86
00:05:45,399 --> 00:05:46,800
She even forced me to sign

87
00:05:48,279 --> 00:05:49,959
an agreement waiving my custody rights.

88
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,040
I truly thought

89
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:52,680
I'd never see that child again

90
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,959
and that she had nothing to do with me.

91
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:56,839
Then just last month,

92
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,800
she suddenly called me.

93
00:06:01,839 --> 00:06:03,480
She said because of the financial crisis over there,

94
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,199
she went bankrupt.

95
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,079
The bank foreclosed on their house,

96
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,240
leaving my daughter nowhere to stay.

97
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,639
She said she was sending the kid back here

98
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:13,920
so I could look after her for a while.

99
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,120
The kid's name is Zhao Jiaqi.

100
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,439
She's 14 this year,

101
00:06:19,319 --> 00:06:20,920
about the same age as our Zhenzhu.

102
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,079
Every word I said is the truth.

103
00:06:23,079 --> 00:06:23,800
That's the whole story.

104
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,279
Dad is sick.

105
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,800
Why didn't you tell me?

106
00:06:32,319 --> 00:06:33,680
Dad didn't tell me either.

107
00:06:36,639 --> 00:06:37,519
He's been avoiding me.

108
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:41,959
I talked to your second brother.

109
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:44,720
The two of us talked it over

110
00:06:46,079 --> 00:06:48,120
and felt we should respect the old man's wishes

111
00:06:49,439 --> 00:06:50,319
and wait for him to bring it up.

112
00:06:52,319 --> 00:06:54,160
I guess he just can't face

113
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,959
the fact that he has late-stage cancer.

114
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:01,000
How could this happen?

115
00:07:05,279 --> 00:07:06,959
Will it be like with Mom?

116
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:09,399
No, not at all.

117
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:10,920
Get away from me!

118
00:07:27,639 --> 00:07:28,319
No, it won't.

119
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:37,079
It won't.

120
00:07:51,879 --> 00:07:53,519
No, it won't. It won't.

121
00:07:53,519 --> 00:07:54,480
It'll get better.

122
00:07:56,879 --> 00:07:57,560
It's going to be okay.

123
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:58,959
Everything will be okay.

124
00:08:11,839 --> 00:08:12,759
Lao Si,

125
00:08:13,879 --> 00:08:14,240
Dad.

126
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,399
Are you asleep?

127
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,439
Not yet.

128
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,839
Why do you sound so weak?

129
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,839
Are you feeling all right?

130
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,639
I'll come home to see you in a couple of days.

131
00:08:35,559 --> 00:08:36,080
How come...

132
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,360
From the sound of your voice...

133
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:39,879
Have you been crying?

134
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:43,399
No.

135
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:49,799
Dad,

136
00:08:50,879 --> 00:08:51,840
take good care of yourself,

137
00:08:52,759 --> 00:08:54,240
and hold our family together.

138
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,279
We can't end up like the Ma family.

139
00:08:58,799 --> 00:08:59,440
Lao Si,

140
00:09:00,879 --> 00:09:03,000
are you hiding something from me?

141
00:09:04,519 --> 00:09:05,200
Lao Si,

142
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:08,159
Dad loves you the most.

143
00:09:08,679 --> 00:09:11,559
You can't lie to me along with them.

144
00:09:16,879 --> 00:09:17,279
Dad...

145
00:09:20,559 --> 00:09:22,879
Sai Duoxi couldn't believe what his daughter said,

146
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,919
but she would never lie to him.

147
00:09:27,799 --> 00:09:29,120
It seemed this family...

148
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,080
they were hell-bent on splitting up.

149
00:09:53,679 --> 00:09:54,480
Xiuliang's here.

150
00:09:54,919 --> 00:09:56,080
Let's order first.

151
00:09:56,279 --> 00:09:57,000
We can talk while we eat.

152
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,279
Big Brother still has some things to handle at the site.

153
00:09:58,279 --> 00:09:59,039
Eat? How can you eat?!

154
00:09:59,039 --> 00:10:00,039
You still have the nerve to eat?

155
00:10:00,759 --> 00:10:02,360
Can't hide your true colors anymore, can you?

156
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:03,600
You want to divide the family?

157
00:10:04,679 --> 00:10:05,840
What right do you have to divide the family?

158
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,840
Whose family are you trying to split up?

159
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,000
Do you have that authority?

160
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:09,759
Let me make this crystal clear:

161
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,799
The old man and I negotiated the demolition payout.

162
00:10:11,799 --> 00:10:13,879
The old man and Big Brother run the construction team.

163
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:14,759
Sure,

164
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,200
you run the household well,

165
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,720
but the old man hasn't shortchanged you either.

166
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:18,639
He gave you living expenses

167
00:10:18,639 --> 00:10:19,679
and let you manage the money!

168
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:20,679
What gives you the right

169
00:10:20,679 --> 00:10:22,000
to drive a wedge between us brothers,

170
00:10:22,159 --> 00:10:23,759
using Big Brother's name to divide this family?

171
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,840
I didn't... I didn't!

172
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,960
Still acting? "I didn't"?

173
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:27,840
Whether you did or not,

174
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:28,759
you know best in your heart!

175
00:10:28,919 --> 00:10:30,399
You took advantage of Big Brother's meek nature

176
00:10:30,399 --> 00:10:31,519
and treated him like a pushover!

177
00:10:31,519 --> 00:10:33,279
If you tell him to go east, he won't dare go west!

178
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,960
How have we treated you all this time?

179
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,600
It was all out of respect for Big Brother!

180
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,080
Did you really think we had no complaints about you?

181
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,159
A hen flaps its wings in a tree,

182
00:10:40,159 --> 00:10:41,279
and you actually think you're a phoenix?

183
00:10:41,279 --> 00:10:42,000
Sai Xiuliang!

184
00:10:42,679 --> 00:10:44,159
Just because you got a little more schooling,

185
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,720
you think you can look down on everyone?

186
00:10:45,879 --> 00:10:47,480
Stop playing dumb when you know full well!

187
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,960
You're full of pure selfishness!

188
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,120
Who are you putting on a show for?

189
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,679
If Dad hadn't favored you,

190
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,879
if Dad hadn't prioritized you in everything,

191
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,919
this family would've been split up long ago!

192
00:10:56,159 --> 00:10:56,919
Everyone came here today,

193
00:10:57,159 --> 00:10:58,960
wasn't it to put everything on the table?

194
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,159
Did I hit a nerve?

195
00:11:01,159 --> 00:11:02,559
You're throwing such a fit here!

196
00:11:02,799 --> 00:11:03,960
How am I throwing a fit?

197
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,200
What kind of act is this?

198
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,720
We haven't even talked business, and you're already brawling!

199
00:11:11,039 --> 00:11:13,320
You want everything out on the table,

200
00:11:13,679 --> 00:11:14,799
made crystal clear.

201
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,519
Fine, I'll make it crystal clear to you today!

202
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,360
Resigning to open a law firm is set in stone.

203
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,840
Not even God himself can stop me!

204
00:11:21,759 --> 00:11:22,720
Let me tell you,

205
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,039
people like you,

206
00:11:24,039 --> 00:11:26,000
who can only see your own little turf,

207
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,279
obsessing every day over demolition money

208
00:11:27,279 --> 00:11:28,399
and the construction team—

209
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,360
is it even worth my breath?

210
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,000
Even if I explained, would you understand?

211
00:11:31,559 --> 00:11:32,279
I have just one thing to say:

212
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,200
this family

213
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:34,000
cannot be divided!

214
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:35,000
And this money—

215
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,159
nobody touches it!

216
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,440
Sai Xiuliang, you've really opened my eyes today!

217
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:39,679
You educated people,

218
00:11:39,679 --> 00:11:40,960
even when acting like thugs, you act so righteous!

219
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:41,320
Second Brother,

220
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:43,440
I had no idea you were so powerful now,

221
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,000
that you can call all the shots in this family.

222
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:45,840
Let me ask you first:

223
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:46,759
what trick are you pulling now?

224
00:11:46,759 --> 00:11:47,600
Playing both sides, huh?

225
00:11:47,799 --> 00:11:49,320
On one hand, you pissed off the old man by quitting.

226
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,000
On the other,

227
00:11:50,159 --> 00:11:50,480
Dad!

228
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,440
Now you're playing the dutiful son!

229
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,120
What are you after?

230
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:52,919
I'm not after anything.

231
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:53,960
I'm not acting like a thug.

232
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:54,919
I just have right on my side!

233
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:56,279
Bottom line, this family cannot be divided.

234
00:11:56,279 --> 00:11:57,000
And then?

235
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,519
Keep all the money for yourself, right?

236
00:11:58,519 --> 00:11:59,759
I think that's exactly what Dad intends.

237
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:01,360
That's why we need to have a proper talk today.

238
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,759
What is there left to talk about?

239
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,360
What is there to divide?

240
00:12:09,639 --> 00:12:11,000
Dad has cancer!

241
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,559
And you're still thinking about splitting money?

242
00:12:12,559 --> 00:12:13,919
Are you even human?!

243
00:12:16,879 --> 00:12:17,759
Why don't you want to divide it?

244
00:12:18,639 --> 00:12:20,480
Because both you and Jin Jingran know!

245
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:45,320
Stop it.

246
00:12:45,759 --> 00:12:47,080
Stop joking. What are you talking about?

247
00:12:48,159 --> 00:12:50,000
Dad has... has cancer.

248
00:12:57,519 --> 00:12:57,960
Late-stage.

249
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:01,120
Last week...

250
00:13:02,919 --> 00:13:03,559
...he was diagnosed.

251
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:07,759
Those test results...

252
00:13:08,919 --> 00:13:09,720
...were Dad's.

253
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:15,799
I'm getting a divorce.

254
00:13:17,279 --> 00:13:18,240
I'm going home.

255
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,320
I'm done with Jin Jingran.

256
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,200
I'm going home to be with Dad.

257
00:13:22,519 --> 00:13:22,879
Come on.

258
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:24,879
Lao Si, don't make things worse right now.

259
00:13:24,879 --> 00:13:25,639
Can you just calm down?

260
00:13:25,639 --> 00:13:26,759
How am I making things worse?

261
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:28,440
Jin Jingran had a daughter all along!

262
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,919
You knew it all along, didn't you?

263
00:13:30,159 --> 00:13:31,080
Why did you keep it from me?

264
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:31,519
It was Dad...

265
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:31,960
Lao Er.

266
00:13:32,279 --> 00:13:33,080
Why didn't you say anything?

267
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:34,480
You knew. Why didn't you say anything?

268
00:13:34,679 --> 00:13:35,799
Why didn't you tell me?

269
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:37,039
Stop arguing, all of you!

270
00:13:37,039 --> 00:13:38,039
You did it on purpose!

271
00:13:40,639 --> 00:13:41,360
Dad is sick!

272
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:43,399
You... you knew, but said nothing!

273
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:43,759
Then...

274
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:47,000
Why didn't... why didn't Dad say anything either?

275
00:13:57,639 --> 00:13:58,879
Now that I know,

276
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,159
it's not too late.

277
00:14:06,559 --> 00:14:08,240
If Qianjin hadn't told me,

278
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:11,480
I'd never have known it was this lively here today.

279
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:31,519
Take a look, all of you.

280
00:14:33,679 --> 00:14:33,960
Dad...

281
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:36,960
We're on the job site together every day,

282
00:14:38,519 --> 00:14:39,440
yet I didn't notice a thing.

283
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:40,919
As your son,

284
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:42,200
I've been completely oblivious.

285
00:14:42,639 --> 00:14:43,720
You didn't know,

286
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:46,480
but someone sure did.

287
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,600
Claiming you didn't know I was sick,

288
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,960
yet you dare try to divide the family?

289
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,039
Dad, Dad!

290
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:55,879
Tell me,

291
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:57,480
how do you plan to split the money?

292
00:14:58,840 --> 00:14:59,679
How are you going to split the family?

293
00:14:59,799 --> 00:15:00,080
Dad...

294
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:01,960
I really didn't know.

295
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,120
If I had known, I...

296
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:05,600
I'd be utterly heartless!

297
00:15:06,879 --> 00:15:07,240
Dad,

298
00:15:07,519 --> 00:15:09,320
we were only discussing it today.

299
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,200
We never said we'd split things up.

300
00:15:10,519 --> 00:15:11,519
Dad, the most important thing right now

301
00:15:11,519 --> 00:15:13,360
is getting to the hospital to see Jin Jingran.

302
00:15:13,639 --> 00:15:15,360
We need to talk about getting you treated.

303
00:15:15,799 --> 00:15:18,000
That day we were at the teahouse,

304
00:15:18,879 --> 00:15:19,759
you already knew,

305
00:15:20,159 --> 00:15:20,480
didn't you?

306
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,639
You kept your mouth shut,

307
00:15:23,399 --> 00:15:25,039
just waiting for today's show!

308
00:15:25,279 --> 00:15:25,559
Dad...

309
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,679
Do you even know what filial piety means?

310
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:29,240
To you, being filial

311
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,840
just means wishing I'd drop dead sooner,

312
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:32,919
so you can take the money!

313
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,159
No, Dad, Dad!

314
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,759
We definitely didn't mean that!

315
00:15:37,399 --> 00:15:38,320
Don't misunderstand!

316
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,320
Misunderstand?

317
00:15:40,799 --> 00:15:42,200
Look at every single one of you!

318
00:15:44,799 --> 00:15:46,200
Cutting corners,

319
00:15:46,639 --> 00:15:47,960
stabbing each other in the back,

320
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,159
unable to keep your own husband in check,

321
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:52,519
and you!

322
00:15:52,879 --> 00:15:55,720
Idling around all day, swindling and cheating!

323
00:15:56,279 --> 00:15:57,840
You can't just scold us!

324
00:15:58,279 --> 00:15:58,960
What about him?

325
00:15:59,159 --> 00:15:59,639
He quit his job!

326
00:15:59,639 --> 00:16:00,679
You should be scolding him, too!

327
00:16:00,679 --> 00:16:01,879
Since you knew all along,

328
00:16:01,879 --> 00:16:02,840
why didn't you tell me?

329
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:05,000
Kicking him while he's down, and you feel justified?

330
00:16:10,639 --> 00:16:11,320
Go on, speak up, all of you!

331
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,080
No one's talking, huh?

332
00:16:26,039 --> 00:16:27,240
Then let me make my stance clear.

333
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
If you want to split up the family,

334
00:16:38,279 --> 00:16:39,279
wait until I'm dead.

335
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:51,519
Dad!

336
00:16:53,759 --> 00:16:54,879
Wait for me, Dad!

337
00:16:55,039 --> 00:16:56,720
Dad, wait for me! Dad!

338
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:03,639
Dad! Dad, wait for me, Dad!

339
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,160
I have to ask you something!

340
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:09,680
Watch out for the cars!

341
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:12,359
Dad! Dad, don't leave!

342
00:17:12,359 --> 00:17:13,839
Dad, get out of the car!

343
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,519
Tell me why, Dad!

344
00:17:15,519 --> 00:17:17,039
Qianjin, this isn't the time to talk to Dad!

345
00:17:17,039 --> 00:17:17,759
Let Dad leave first!

346
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,200
It's dangerous! Step back!

347
00:17:19,279 --> 00:17:19,839
Enough!

348
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:20,279
Dad!

349
00:17:20,599 --> 00:17:20,880
Dad!

350
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:22,039
Let go of me!

351
00:17:22,519 --> 00:17:24,440
Dad! Dad, don't leave!

352
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,039
Watch the car!

353
00:17:25,039 --> 00:17:25,440
Dad!

354
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:26,640
Dad!

355
00:17:27,079 --> 00:17:27,519
Dad!

356
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,519
Dad!

357
00:17:29,039 --> 00:17:29,440
Dad!

358
00:17:32,759 --> 00:17:33,640
Second Brother, don't you walk away!

359
00:17:34,119 --> 00:17:35,640
Second Brother, you're no good either!

360
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:37,759
You and Jin Jingran are both bastards!

361
00:17:37,839 --> 00:17:39,440
You're the one who introduced us!

362
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:40,680
As if you didn't know!

363
00:17:40,759 --> 00:17:42,400
I knew. So what if I did?

364
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:43,400
Has Jin Jingran treated you badly?

365
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,319
Think about it carefully.

366
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,079
Look at a guy like Jin Jingran—

367
00:17:45,079 --> 00:17:46,440
an associate chief physician with a bright future.

368
00:17:46,559 --> 00:17:47,079
And what are you?

369
00:17:47,079 --> 00:17:48,279
You couldn't even get into college!

370
00:17:48,519 --> 00:17:49,119
To everyone else,

371
00:17:49,119 --> 00:17:49,920
you married way out of your league!

372
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:50,440
Don't you get that?

373
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:51,519
So you thought you could just

374
00:17:51,519 --> 00:17:52,680
sell me out like this, didn't you?

375
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:53,599
What do you mean, "sell you out"?

376
00:17:53,599 --> 00:17:55,039
Did I take any money, or did Dad?

377
00:17:55,119 --> 00:17:56,279
If his daughter hadn't come back,

378
00:17:56,279 --> 00:17:57,000
you wouldn't know a thing.

379
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,440
Wouldn't you still be living in peace?

380
00:17:58,680 --> 00:17:59,559
Just think about Ma Laijiao!

381
00:17:59,759 --> 00:18:00,680
What more could you possibly want?

382
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,359
Even so, you had no right to lie to me like this!

383
00:18:02,359 --> 00:18:03,519
None of you are even human!

384
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:05,240
I don't care! I'm divorcing him!

385
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:05,599
Sis!

386
00:18:05,839 --> 00:18:07,680
Come on, get up! Get up!

387
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,160
Get up!

388
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,160
With all these people watching, have some shame!

389
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:10,000
Get up!

390
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:10,559
Sai Qianjin!

391
00:18:11,119 --> 00:18:11,720
Let me tell you something.

392
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:13,359
Right now you have no money and no job.

393
00:18:13,359 --> 00:18:14,000
How do you expect to get a divorce?

394
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:14,640
How could you possibly divorce him?

395
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:15,720
Dad is sick right now.

396
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,039
He needs Jin Jingran's connections.

397
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,119
It's a crucial moment, do you hear me?

398
00:18:18,599 --> 00:18:19,519
Don't make a scene at a time like this!

399
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:21,160
Second Brother, you had bad intentions all along!

400
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:23,240
Everything happening to me today is your fault!

401
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:23,920
Fine, fine!

402
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:24,640
Just tell me,

403
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:25,880
where are you staying tonight?

404
00:18:26,079 --> 00:18:26,799
I'm going home.

405
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,079
Qingyangli.

406
00:18:28,519 --> 00:18:29,359
I'm going to see Dad!

407
00:18:29,359 --> 00:18:30,160
I've been talking to you all this time,

408
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:30,920
and it was all for nothing?

409
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:55,759
Dad,

410
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,920
this was all an accident!

411
00:18:58,160 --> 00:18:59,720
What did you promise me back then?

412
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:00,799
Didn't you say

413
00:19:00,799 --> 00:19:02,359
she took the kid to America

414
00:19:02,359 --> 00:19:03,400
and was never coming back?

415
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,480
That's what she said back then!

416
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:05,359
Then what's happening now?

417
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:06,279
How was I supposed to know?

418
00:19:06,279 --> 00:19:07,880
Some financial crisis hit over in the US.

419
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,359
Her mom went broke and wanted to jump,

420
00:19:09,599 --> 00:19:10,680
so she insisted on sending the kid back!

421
00:19:10,839 --> 00:19:12,000
And just like that, the kid showed up!

422
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,079
What was I supposed to do?

423
00:19:13,079 --> 00:19:14,680
Spare me that bullshit!

424
00:19:14,839 --> 00:19:16,200
Now that the kid is back,

425
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,079
what do you plan to do?

426
00:19:17,559 --> 00:19:19,279
How is Qianjin supposed to take this?

427
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:20,920
How can she not hate me?

428
00:19:27,359 --> 00:19:28,039
Can you resolve this?

429
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:29,440
If you can't,

430
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,720
I'll pack up her things tomorrow,

431
00:19:30,839 --> 00:19:31,279
and you're getting a divorce!

432
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:32,480
Dad!

433
00:19:33,599 --> 00:19:35,039
Can you stop threatening divorce all the time?

434
00:19:35,119 --> 00:19:36,160
Just give me a little more time.

435
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:41,799
Then come home with me right now

436
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:43,680
and take Qianjin back.

437
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,519
My shift ends in half an hour.

438
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:47,880
Wait for me,

439
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:48,480
and I'll go with you.

440
00:20:06,559 --> 00:20:06,839
Dad,

441
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:08,960
how's your condition?

442
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:10,680
What did the doctor say?

443
00:20:11,519 --> 00:20:12,359
Did they give any advice?

444
00:20:17,039 --> 00:20:17,960
What do you think

445
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,720
we should do?

446
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:21,839
It's not my specialty,

447
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:23,759
so I can't say for sure.

448
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,640
But I don't think we can delay it.

449
00:20:26,039 --> 00:20:27,640
If you're not confident about Honggang,

450
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:29,680
we can go to Beijing or Shanghai.

451
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,680
How much would that even cost?

452
00:20:32,039 --> 00:20:33,720
Dad, money doesn't matter.

453
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,519
Your health is what matters.

454
00:20:39,319 --> 00:20:40,200
It's good like this now.

455
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,000
We've cleared the air.

456
00:20:43,599 --> 00:20:44,519
We're family.

457
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,400
We can sit down and talk it through.

458
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:49,279
Over money,

459
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,599
every single one of them turns on me.

460
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,519
What's there left to discuss?

461
00:20:57,079 --> 00:20:58,319
Everything's been said plainly.

462
00:20:59,559 --> 00:21:01,079
Everything's out in the open.

463
00:21:02,799 --> 00:21:04,200
This whole big family,

464
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:07,400
used to hiding behind pretenses,

465
00:21:08,839 --> 00:21:10,720
now that we've laid ourselves bare,

466
00:21:12,079 --> 00:21:14,039
none of us can even face each other.

467
00:21:29,319 --> 00:21:30,039
Xiuming,

468
00:21:31,559 --> 00:21:32,119
do you believe me?

469
00:21:33,039 --> 00:21:34,960
I really didn't know Dad was sick.

470
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:37,960
If I had known,

471
00:21:42,759 --> 00:21:43,880
if I had known even a little,

472
00:21:45,319 --> 00:21:47,279
I would never have done this.

473
00:21:47,279 --> 00:21:48,079
Is that what I'm angry about?

474
00:21:48,839 --> 00:21:49,880
Is that what I'm mad about?

475
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,200
Only when I got to the restaurant today

476
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,160
did I find out what you were doing!

477
00:21:52,759 --> 00:21:53,640
Did you tell me before setting this up?

478
00:21:54,039 --> 00:21:55,200
Who did you consult before arranging this?

479
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:57,279
No, really, I didn't organize it today.

480
00:21:57,279 --> 00:21:58,640
Second Brother set it up today.

481
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,599
Don't bring up Second Brother to me!

482
00:22:00,119 --> 00:22:00,759
Whenever you mention him,

483
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:01,720
it makes my blood boil!

484
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:02,759
He knew Dad was sick, right?

485
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:03,920
He knew Dad was sick,

486
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:04,960
so why didn't he tell me?

487
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,039
Is he the only son?

488
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,000
Am I not a son, too?

489
00:22:07,480 --> 00:22:08,960
He teamed up with Jin Jingran

490
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:09,960
to keep this from me!

491
00:22:10,599 --> 00:22:11,640
And as for this Jin Jingran,

492
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:12,680
married for how many years now,

493
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,359
and he has a kid on the side!

494
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,440
Second Brother knew.

495
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:17,400
Dad knew.

496
00:22:17,400 --> 00:22:18,720
Turns out I was the only one in the dark!

497
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,519
I didn't know either!

498
00:22:21,359 --> 00:22:22,680
Jin Jingran lied to me,

499
00:22:22,759 --> 00:22:23,759
Second Brother lied to me,

500
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:24,599
and fine if Dad lied to me,

501
00:22:24,599 --> 00:22:25,799
but now you're lying to me too!

502
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:26,480
In this family,

503
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:27,799
am I that incapable of handling things?

504
00:22:28,039 --> 00:22:29,000
What kind of eldest brother am I?

505
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:29,839
What kind of eldest brother am I?!

506
00:22:29,839 --> 00:22:30,799
Then what about me?

507
00:22:31,599 --> 00:22:32,839
I don't count for anything at all!

508
00:22:34,200 --> 00:22:35,519
Right now in Second Brother's eyes,

509
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:38,680
I'm just a backstabbing, wicked sister-in-law!

510
00:22:39,359 --> 00:22:40,720
Third Brother treats me like a traitor!

511
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:43,039
Fourth Brother says I made Dad sick with anger!

512
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:44,200
I don't mean a thing to anyone!

513
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:45,359
I'm wrong everywhere I turn!

514
00:22:45,680 --> 00:22:47,240
I get blamed by everyone, inside and out! I...

515
00:22:57,799 --> 00:22:58,240
In that room.

516
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:02,960
Dad.

517
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:16,799
Brother,

518
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:19,079
I don't even know what to say to you.

519
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,359
You... you guys just suit yourselves, then.

520
00:23:35,839 --> 00:23:36,240
Qianjin.

521
00:23:38,079 --> 00:23:38,880
Who told you to come here?

522
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:40,079
I'm here to pick you up.

523
00:23:42,759 --> 00:23:43,079
Qianjin.

524
00:23:43,079 --> 00:23:43,640
Get out.

525
00:23:43,720 --> 00:23:44,880
Qianjin, Qianjin, listen to me.

526
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:45,359
Listen to me.

527
00:23:45,359 --> 00:23:46,279
Get out of here.

528
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:02,400
Qianjin

529
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,559
All these years,

530
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:16,480
I never meant to hide it from you.

531
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,400
It was Dad and Second Brother—

532
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:22,000
they told me not to say anything.

533
00:24:22,799 --> 00:24:24,400
I really did want to marry you,

534
00:24:25,039 --> 00:24:26,359
so I just listened to them.

535
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:28,440
So...

536
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:32,000
you all teamed up to lie to me,

537
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:32,920
is that it?

538
00:24:33,799 --> 00:24:34,480
Let's talk at home,

539
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:35,240
okay?

540
00:24:36,079 --> 00:24:36,480
I'm not going back.

541
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:38,720
This is my home.

542
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:41,680
We're married now.

543
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:43,240
We have our own home.

544
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:45,119
If you stay at your parents' place,

545
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:46,799
and people find out,

546
00:24:46,799 --> 00:24:48,119
they're going to gossip.

547
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:50,240
You have to think of Dad too,

548
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:50,799
don't you?

549
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:51,720
Besides,

550
00:24:52,359 --> 00:24:53,480
Dad isn't in good health.

551
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:55,359
There are still so many things

552
00:24:55,359 --> 00:24:56,279
we'll have to take care of later.

553
00:25:05,079 --> 00:25:05,480
Qianjin.

554
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:07,759
Qianjin,

555
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:09,359
look at this bed.

556
00:25:09,759 --> 00:25:10,200
It's so hard.

557
00:25:11,160 --> 00:25:11,839
How can you sleep on this?

558
00:25:12,119 --> 00:25:13,119
And your room is on the ground floor.

559
00:25:13,319 --> 00:25:14,359
There's a chicken coop right outside.

560
00:25:14,880 --> 00:25:15,920
They'll crow before dawn.

561
00:25:16,519 --> 00:25:17,519
You won't get any rest at all.

562
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:18,720
And your skincare products—

563
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,160
look, the bottles are all empty.

564
00:25:21,279 --> 00:25:22,799
You can't go upstairs to borrow from Sister-in-law.

565
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:24,279
Never mind how awkward that is,

566
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:26,160
the brands she uses—

567
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:27,559
are you even used to them?

568
00:25:28,559 --> 00:25:29,519
Aren't you worried about having a reaction?

569
00:25:39,759 --> 00:25:40,720
That's enough from you.

570
00:25:41,319 --> 00:25:41,799
You're drunk.

571
00:25:41,799 --> 00:25:42,759
In a bit, no one's gonna look after you.

572
00:25:44,079 --> 00:25:44,759
Hey, nephew.

573
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:47,319
Is this act for your dad,

574
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:48,880
or 'cause you can't get any money?

575
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,400
Can't it be both?

576
00:25:51,079 --> 00:25:51,359
Look,

577
00:25:51,759 --> 00:25:54,680
finding out the old man has cancer today...

578
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:56,119
It scared me to death.

579
00:25:56,119 --> 00:25:58,400
How could he get so sick?

580
00:25:58,480 --> 00:25:59,839
What if they can't cure him?

581
00:25:59,839 --> 00:26:00,559
What do I do?

582
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:02,799
I feel so awful inside.

583
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:05,200
Then you say there's no money to split,

584
00:26:05,200 --> 00:26:08,000
and that makes me feel even worse.

585
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,440
Why did he

586
00:26:09,480 --> 00:26:12,319
have to get sick at this crucial moment?

587
00:26:12,319 --> 00:26:14,559
Talk about bad luck!

588
00:26:14,680 --> 00:26:16,759
If you ask me, money is money and dad is dad.

589
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:18,279
You still gotta ask for it.

590
00:26:18,359 --> 00:26:20,079
Give me a break.

591
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:22,480
He already cusses me out every day,

592
00:26:22,559 --> 00:26:24,240
calling me an ungrateful brat

593
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:26,359
and a good-for-nothing moocher.

594
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:29,599
If I ask to split the money now,

595
00:26:29,599 --> 00:26:31,920
he'll tear me to shreds!

596
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:36,599
He'll call me the worst son in Qingyangli.

597
00:26:37,279 --> 00:26:38,720
You can't be filial without money anyway.

598
00:26:39,039 --> 00:26:40,920
You usually act like a slacker,

599
00:26:41,160 --> 00:26:42,720
but who knew you really cared about your dad.

600
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:43,240
Laibu,

601
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:44,279
got any good ideas?

602
00:26:44,279 --> 00:26:45,000
Let's help him out.

603
00:26:45,119 --> 00:26:46,359
Look, this cancer thing

604
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:48,000
isn't as bad as you think.

605
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:49,240
Let me educate you a bit.

606
00:26:49,599 --> 00:26:50,599
What is cancer?

607
00:26:50,920 --> 00:26:53,319
Cancer starts as a bad cell.

608
00:26:53,839 --> 00:26:55,519
It grows inside your body,

609
00:26:55,519 --> 00:26:57,000
and becomes a tumor.

610
00:26:57,279 --> 00:26:58,519
That tumor is cancer.

611
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,039
You gotta try Chinese medicine.

612
00:27:00,359 --> 00:27:00,720
Right?

613
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:04,160
Expel the evil, strengthen the foundation.

614
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:06,400
That actually makes some sense.

615
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:07,960
Thanks, buddy.

616
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:08,920
Bottoms up.

617
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:09,359
We're brothers.

618
00:27:15,079 --> 00:27:16,079
You're really in your feelings today!

619
00:27:16,599 --> 00:27:17,839
What're you laughing at?

620
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:18,960
I'm laughing at you.

621
00:27:21,359 --> 00:27:22,400
Come on, stop crying.

622
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:24,039
Ma Laibu, go settle the bill,

623
00:27:24,039 --> 00:27:24,599
then take him home.

624
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:25,119
Don't worry.

625
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:25,960
Thanks.

626
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:26,880
We're buddies.

627
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:28,000
It's nothing.

628
00:27:28,559 --> 00:27:28,960
Buddy.

629
00:27:39,599 --> 00:27:39,920
Qianjin!

630
00:27:41,799 --> 00:27:43,000
Qian— Qianjin— Qian—

631
00:27:46,799 --> 00:27:47,160
Dad!

632
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:49,039
I know what you meant.

633
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:50,880
I listened to you

634
00:27:51,799 --> 00:27:52,720
and went back with him!

635
00:27:54,319 --> 00:27:54,960
But

636
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:57,000
how could you lie to me?

637
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,599
And you lied to me for so long!

638
00:28:07,720 --> 00:28:08,240
Open the door!

639
00:28:08,759 --> 00:28:09,279
I want to see you!

640
00:28:12,079 --> 00:28:13,200
Dad, I said open the door!

641
00:28:13,200 --> 00:28:14,400
Just let me say a few words,

642
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:15,720
and I'll leave, okay?

643
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:19,720
Dad, please open the door, okay?

644
00:28:19,799 --> 00:28:20,880
Open the door!

645
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:21,279
Qianjin.

646
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:23,519
Dad's already asleep.

647
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:24,799
Old Sai!

648
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:26,759
I know you're hiding from me!

649
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:29,519
I'm telling you, I'm mad!

650
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:32,640
I hate you!

651
00:28:33,119 --> 00:28:34,359
Dad, you have to get checked!

652
00:28:34,559 --> 00:28:35,000
Once I've set it up,

653
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:35,680
I'll call you.

654
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:36,799
Qianjin.

655
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:38,759
Qianjin!

656
00:28:50,599 --> 00:28:51,160
Get in.

657
00:29:17,119 --> 00:29:17,519
Jiao.

658
00:29:19,559 --> 00:29:20,039
Big Brother.

659
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:21,759
What brings you here?

660
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,160
I stopped by your place earlier.

661
00:29:23,319 --> 00:29:24,440
Your dad said you weren't home yet.

662
00:29:25,599 --> 00:29:26,359
Why aren't you off work yet?

663
00:29:27,200 --> 00:29:28,200
I'm on an IV drip here.

664
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:28,960
It's not done yet.

665
00:29:29,720 --> 00:29:30,400
Did you need something?

666
00:29:37,240 --> 00:29:38,319
With Number Four kicking up such a fuss,

667
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:39,440
I can understand it.

668
00:29:40,319 --> 00:29:41,920
If Jin Jingran had come clean back then,

669
00:29:43,039 --> 00:29:44,519
he wouldn't have been able to marry her.

670
00:29:45,359 --> 00:29:46,440
The reason I came to you...

671
00:29:47,759 --> 00:29:49,640
is to ask you to help talk to her.

672
00:29:50,599 --> 00:29:52,960
We should help them make up, not break up, right?

673
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:55,519
Since he's already married into our family,

674
00:29:55,519 --> 00:29:56,519
he's family now.

675
00:29:57,559 --> 00:29:59,480
Besides, it's not a deal-breaker.

676
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:02,559
If this had happened during their marriage,

677
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:04,799
then Jin Jingran would be in the wrong.

678
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,359
But after all, this was...

679
00:30:08,039 --> 00:30:09,359
something that happened before marriage.

680
00:30:10,799 --> 00:30:11,960
I can completely understand.

681
00:30:13,839 --> 00:30:14,640
He just...

682
00:30:15,599 --> 00:30:16,960
wanted to treat Qianjin well.

683
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:17,759
Right?

684
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:24,400
As for me,

685
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:25,839
I've been thinking about it for a long time,

686
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:28,920
and felt I could only turn to you.

687
00:30:29,519 --> 00:30:30,759
All the reasoning I just laid out...

688
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:32,519
only if you tell Qianjin,

689
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,279
might she actually take it to heart.

690
00:30:37,759 --> 00:30:38,839
She's so lucky.

691
00:30:42,920 --> 00:30:43,480
Who's lucky?

692
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:45,680
Qianjin.

693
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:49,079
What's so lucky about Qianjin?

694
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:51,279
She has a dad who loves her,

695
00:30:52,759 --> 00:30:53,839
a husband who dotes on her,

696
00:30:55,519 --> 00:30:57,160
and a big brother looking out for her.

697
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:00,279
Isn't that lucky?

698
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:01,920
What kind of big brother am I?

699
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:04,000
Jin Jingran...

700
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:05,839
didn't tell me,

701
00:31:07,839 --> 00:31:08,519
which I can understand.

702
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:10,480
But Dad and Second Brother...

703
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:11,359
why didn't they tell me either?

704
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:13,799
Do I even count in this family—

705
00:31:13,799 --> 00:31:14,400
Blood is backing up into the IV!

706
00:31:14,839 --> 00:31:15,799
Quick, help me check it!

707
00:31:18,359 --> 00:31:19,599
I... I don't know what to—

708
00:31:25,720 --> 00:31:27,200
What kind of big brother? Some big brother...

709
00:31:43,759 --> 00:31:44,119
Qianjin.

710
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:44,720
Um...

711
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:45,079
What?

712
00:31:46,160 --> 00:31:47,400
There's something I want to tell you.

713
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:48,039
Go ahead.

714
00:31:49,759 --> 00:31:50,279
Well...

715
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:56,559
I brought Zhao Jiaqi home to stay with us.

716
00:31:59,759 --> 00:32:00,640
What did you say?

717
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:01,720
Say that again.

718
00:32:02,480 --> 00:32:03,839
I brought Jiaqi home to stay with us.

719
00:32:04,079 --> 00:32:05,559
Jin Jingran, are you crazy?

720
00:32:05,559 --> 00:32:05,880
No, listen.

721
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:06,759
Think about it.

722
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:07,960
With her mom's current situation,

723
00:32:08,319 --> 00:32:09,839
she... she can't go back anytime soon.

724
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:11,240
She's such a young girl.

725
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:11,759
Leaving her staying outside alone,

726
00:32:12,359 --> 00:32:13,640
I was really worried.

727
00:32:13,759 --> 00:32:14,160
Wait, Jin Jingran,

728
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:15,400
did you even consider my feelings?

729
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:16,519
Did you think about me at all?

730
00:32:16,519 --> 00:32:18,079
Isn't this me considering your feelings,

731
00:32:18,079 --> 00:32:19,319
by discussing it with you now?

732
00:32:19,319 --> 00:32:20,799
Discussing it? You already let her—

733
00:32:20,839 --> 00:32:22,039
If you don't agree, fine.

734
00:32:22,640 --> 00:32:23,400
I'll tell her right now

735
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:24,559
to go back to the hotel, all right?

736
00:32:24,759 --> 00:32:26,160
Fine, tell her to go back to the hotel.

737
00:32:26,160 --> 00:32:27,000
Right now!

738
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:29,000
Sweetheart...

739
00:32:29,359 --> 00:32:30,480
My dear wife, I'm begging you.

740
00:32:30,480 --> 00:32:31,799
Please be the bigger person, okay?

741
00:32:31,799 --> 00:32:32,799
Just have some pity on the kid.

742
00:32:32,799 --> 00:32:33,640
If she won't leave, I will!

743
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:34,440
Qianjin!

744
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:34,920
Wait!

745
00:32:35,599 --> 00:32:35,839
Come on!

746
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:36,519
Qianjin!

747
00:32:36,960 --> 00:32:37,279
Qianjin!

748
00:32:38,079 --> 00:32:38,640
Qianjin! Qianjin!

749
00:32:39,119 --> 00:32:40,319
Wait, where are you going?

750
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:41,319
Where are you going?

751
00:32:41,319 --> 00:32:42,519
Where am I going? I'm going home!

752
00:32:42,519 --> 00:32:43,640
But you can't go back right now!

753
00:32:43,759 --> 00:32:44,359
When you just left,

754
00:32:44,359 --> 00:32:45,160
what did you promise Dad?

755
00:32:45,160 --> 00:32:46,000
I don't care.

756
00:32:46,160 --> 00:32:47,000
I'm not staying here anyway.

757
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,880
Listen, Dad's health is what matters most right now.

758
00:32:49,039 --> 00:32:50,240
You know that better than I do.

759
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:51,119
I'm swamped during the day too,

760
00:32:51,240 --> 00:32:52,359
finding doctors for Dad

761
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:53,960
and arranging his hospital stay.

762
00:32:54,119 --> 00:32:55,119
Can't our little family just live peacefully

763
00:32:55,119 --> 00:32:56,000
and keep things calm, please?

764
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:57,359
Don't add to Dad's stress.

765
00:32:59,200 --> 00:32:59,680
Okay?

766
00:33:09,799 --> 00:33:10,839
Jiaqi, Jiaqi.

767
00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:12,359
It's too loud.

768
00:33:13,960 --> 00:33:14,519
Hey there.

769
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:17,799
Keep it down.

770
00:33:18,200 --> 00:33:20,200
Why? It's not that loud.

771
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:20,920
No.

772
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:23,079
You're bothering people.

773
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:24,440
This is your place, right?

774
00:33:24,960 --> 00:33:26,119
So now it's my place, too.

775
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:28,839
What's wrong with me playing video games here?

776
00:33:29,119 --> 00:33:30,200
That's fine, but...

777
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:33,279
Go to bed early.

778
00:33:44,799 --> 00:33:46,680
Your bank account balance is

779
00:33:47,079 --> 00:33:50,359
1,297 yuan and 84 cents.

780
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:02,119
Qianjin.

781
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:06,039
What are you looking for?

782
00:34:10,480 --> 00:34:11,280
What are you searching for?

783
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:12,519
Where's my diamond necklace?

784
00:34:13,119 --> 00:34:14,199
Where's the gold bracelet Mom gave me?

785
00:34:14,199 --> 00:34:15,000
Where did you put them?

786
00:34:15,679 --> 00:34:17,239
Last time you said you were worried about thieves,

787
00:34:17,559 --> 00:34:18,800
so you hid them yourself.

788
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:20,719
I definitely didn't take them.

789
00:34:21,599 --> 00:34:22,519
Jiaqi wouldn't take them either.

790
00:34:22,920 --> 00:34:24,079
Did you hide them somewhere and forget?

791
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:26,360
What do you need the gold bracelet for?

792
00:34:28,599 --> 00:34:29,039
Qianjin.

793
00:34:29,599 --> 00:34:30,440
Stop looking, all right?

794
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:32,559
Can you please stop looking?

795
00:34:32,679 --> 00:34:33,639
Just hear me out, okay?

796
00:34:33,719 --> 00:34:34,239
Let go—

797
00:34:34,719 --> 00:34:35,519
Listen to me. Listen to me.

798
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:37,119
Qianjin.

799
00:34:37,199 --> 00:34:38,280
Let go of me!

800
00:34:38,519 --> 00:34:39,079
Qianjin.

801
00:34:39,519 --> 00:34:40,320
At such a crucial moment,

802
00:34:40,719 --> 00:34:42,000
let's not fight, all right?

803
00:34:43,119 --> 00:34:43,599
Please, listen to me.

804
00:34:46,039 --> 00:34:47,000
Here's 10,000 yuan.

805
00:34:48,320 --> 00:34:48,760
Take it.

806
00:34:50,440 --> 00:34:51,440
Dad needs money right now.

807
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:52,079
Take this

808
00:34:53,519 --> 00:34:54,719
and buy Dad something nice.

809
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:56,960
Everything...

810
00:34:57,639 --> 00:34:58,559
I'll take care of it all.

811
00:34:58,960 --> 00:34:59,559
Trust me.

812
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:04,079
It's okay. It's okay.

813
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:05,039
Don't cry. Don't cry.

814
00:35:07,559 --> 00:35:07,960
Don't cry.

815
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:40,639
About the old man's illness,

816
00:35:42,039 --> 00:35:43,079
now that it's out in the open,

817
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:45,440
it's actually for the best.

818
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:51,840
Going forward, between Dad and the law firm,

819
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:53,199
if there's anything you need from me,

820
00:35:53,199 --> 00:35:53,960
just let me know.

821
00:35:54,400 --> 00:35:55,440
I'll help in any way I can.

822
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:00,840
Don't worry.

823
00:36:02,119 --> 00:36:03,199
I'll take care of both sides.

824
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:05,440
I won't let it turn into a mess.

825
00:36:14,360 --> 00:36:16,480
Whether Sai Duoxi's illness could be cured,

826
00:36:17,559 --> 00:36:18,239
how to treat it,

827
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:20,639
how much it would cost,

828
00:36:21,719 --> 00:36:23,079
and whether he would pull through...

829
00:36:24,920 --> 00:36:26,639
No one was there to answer these questions.

830
00:36:28,559 --> 00:36:30,559
Something bigger than money,

831
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:33,800
something far more important surfaced,

832
00:36:35,239 --> 00:36:38,119
weighing so heavily that no one could sleep.

833
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:56,400
Sir,

834
00:36:57,199 --> 00:36:58,559
I'll be straight with you.

835
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:00,639
Regarding the treatment plan,

836
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:01,440
there are two options.

837
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:03,159
Conservative treatment,

838
00:37:03,599 --> 00:37:04,400
or surgery.

839
00:37:05,039 --> 00:37:06,079
With conservative treatment,

840
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:07,159
the risk is low,

841
00:37:07,519 --> 00:37:08,159
there's less pain,

842
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:09,159
and it costs less.

843
00:37:09,320 --> 00:37:10,599
However, the outcome

844
00:37:11,039 --> 00:37:11,719
can't be guaranteed.

845
00:37:12,119 --> 00:37:12,960
As for surgery,

846
00:37:13,039 --> 00:37:13,679
there's more pain,

847
00:37:14,039 --> 00:37:14,679
it costs more,

848
00:37:14,920 --> 00:37:15,719
and the risk is higher.

849
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:16,639
However,

850
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:17,840
it gives him a fighting chance.

851
00:37:19,239 --> 00:37:19,960
Furthermore,

852
00:37:20,079 --> 00:37:20,960
any surgery

853
00:37:21,199 --> 00:37:21,960
comes with risks.

854
00:37:22,199 --> 00:37:23,239
No one can guarantee anything.

855
00:37:23,599 --> 00:37:25,880
Though Professor He Jia is an authority on this.

856
00:37:26,320 --> 00:37:27,039
Across all patient stages,

857
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:28,679
his team achieves

858
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:29,840
an overall survival rate

859
00:37:30,239 --> 00:37:31,880
of up to 78.6%.

860
00:37:32,079 --> 00:37:32,639
78%?

861
00:37:32,920 --> 00:37:34,320
Doesn't that mean two out of ten still die?

862
00:37:35,079 --> 00:37:35,440
Shut up.

863
00:37:36,159 --> 00:37:36,599
Jin Jingran,

864
00:37:36,960 --> 00:37:37,519
let me ask you,

865
00:37:37,760 --> 00:37:39,039
should we operate or not?

866
00:37:39,039 --> 00:37:40,199
Give us a straight answer.

867
00:37:40,280 --> 00:37:41,400
You're a doctor!

868
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:42,000
Keep your voice down.

869
00:37:43,519 --> 00:37:45,000
Whether we operate or not,

870
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:46,960
radiation and chemo are necessary.

871
00:37:47,079 --> 00:37:47,960
This is like a moon landing.

872
00:37:48,239 --> 00:37:49,719
It takes time and it's very difficult.

873
00:37:49,880 --> 00:37:50,960
So we must be prepared

874
00:37:50,960 --> 00:37:52,559
for long-term treatment and care.

875
00:37:54,079 --> 00:37:55,360
I took care of your mom.

876
00:37:57,559 --> 00:37:58,440
I have experience.

877
00:38:09,039 --> 00:38:10,320
I think we should still do the surgery.

878
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:11,199
Even though there are risks,

879
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:12,159
we should give it one last shot.

880
00:38:12,159 --> 00:38:13,360
Surgery?! What if something goes wrong?

881
00:38:13,360 --> 00:38:14,519
Why do you butt into everything? Step aside!

882
00:38:14,679 --> 00:38:15,400
You're putting your hands on me?!

883
00:38:15,480 --> 00:38:16,480
Is it confirmed there are risks?

884
00:38:19,280 --> 00:38:19,599
Dad!

885
00:38:19,840 --> 00:38:20,199
Dad!

886
00:38:27,239 --> 00:38:28,039
Don't follow me.

887
00:38:29,239 --> 00:38:30,360
I'm going to the bathroom.

888
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:42,719
Dad.

889
00:38:45,039 --> 00:38:45,719
Have you made up your mind?

890
00:38:48,320 --> 00:38:50,079
Make a decision already, Dad!

891
00:38:50,559 --> 00:38:51,760
What are you rushing me for?

892
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:01,400
There's something I need to say.

893
00:39:03,119 --> 00:39:03,800
As for me,

894
00:39:05,199 --> 00:39:06,639
I'm planning to sell Changfu.

895
00:39:08,760 --> 00:39:10,159
Going forward, I'm afraid you two

896
00:39:10,559 --> 00:39:11,920
will have to find another living.

897
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,159
Sell it?

898
00:39:13,760 --> 00:39:14,960
You really want to step down?

899
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:15,920
I can't keep going.

900
00:39:16,239 --> 00:39:17,840
It's not that I want to quit.

901
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:19,440
Huzi wants to buy it.

902
00:39:20,440 --> 00:39:20,679
You...

903
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:22,119
did you agree?

904
00:39:23,079 --> 00:39:26,000
Earlier, he wanted me to fire both of you.

905
00:39:26,079 --> 00:39:27,000
I managed to hold him off.

906
00:39:27,320 --> 00:39:29,239
Now he's making an issue out of construction quality.

907
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:31,360
All my old connections have retired.

908
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:32,280
They can't help anymore.

909
00:39:32,760 --> 00:39:33,679
Right now,

910
00:39:34,679 --> 00:39:36,639
even if I want to stand firm, I can't.

911
00:39:38,519 --> 00:39:39,280
I understand.

912
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:41,960
He's coming after me.

913
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:45,079
I've dragged both of you down.

914
00:39:45,159 --> 00:39:46,119
No, don't, Xizi.

915
00:39:46,719 --> 00:39:47,480
Don't say that.

916
00:39:47,679 --> 00:39:50,079
He might not be doing this over what happened 18 years ago.

917
00:39:50,400 --> 00:39:51,480
The situation now is,

918
00:39:51,679 --> 00:39:52,559
something went wrong at the site,

919
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:53,920
and they've got leverage on us.

920
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:55,840
He's a big boss,

921
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:56,639
and we're just small fry.

922
00:39:57,119 --> 00:39:58,039
If we fight him, we can't win.

923
00:39:59,519 --> 00:40:00,320
Forget it.

924
00:40:01,159 --> 00:40:01,920
Once the company is sold,

925
00:40:02,159 --> 00:40:04,000
I'll go abroad to be with my wife and kids.

926
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:11,679
Brother Wei,

927
00:40:13,639 --> 00:40:15,199
let me tell you something, too.

928
00:40:16,719 --> 00:40:17,360
As for me,

929
00:40:18,320 --> 00:40:19,719
I was diagnosed with a serious illness.

930
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:21,280
I have a tumor.

931
00:40:24,280 --> 00:40:25,679
Is it serious? What did the doctor say?

932
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:27,119
It's pretty complicated.

933
00:40:28,079 --> 00:40:28,719
Hard to treat.

934
00:40:29,840 --> 00:40:31,920
I definitely have to be hospitalized.

935
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:35,119
You see Old Ma in his current state,

936
00:40:35,400 --> 00:40:36,480
and my eldest son

937
00:40:37,079 --> 00:40:38,880
is running between both our sites.

938
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:39,840
It can't go on like this.

939
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:41,559
I was thinking, if you

940
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:43,199
can find some time,

941
00:40:43,239 --> 00:40:44,360
keep an eye on things for us, too.

942
00:40:44,480 --> 00:40:45,480
You don't even need to ask.

943
00:40:45,480 --> 00:40:46,079
Of course I will.

944
00:40:48,639 --> 00:40:48,960
Here.

945
00:40:49,719 --> 00:40:50,440
Xizi, no, don't!

946
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:51,159
Don't stop me.

947
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:52,000
This drink,

948
00:40:52,679 --> 00:40:53,079
I have to have it.

949
00:40:56,400 --> 00:40:57,559
I know

950
00:40:57,559 --> 00:41:00,400
what shape my body is in.

951
00:41:01,199 --> 00:41:02,239
I just mean,

952
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:04,599
if anything happens to me,

953
00:41:06,039 --> 00:41:06,840
my family,

954
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:07,840
and the site...

955
00:41:09,519 --> 00:41:11,159
I'm leaving them in your hands.

956
00:41:16,880 --> 00:41:17,239
Old Ma...

957
00:41:17,239 --> 00:41:18,000
Old Ma, Old Ma, Old Ma.

958
00:41:19,039 --> 00:41:19,599
What's with you?

959
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:21,920
At our age,

960
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:23,079
what haven't we been through, right?

961
00:41:23,639 --> 00:41:24,400
If you're fine,

962
00:41:24,400 --> 00:41:26,039
what could happen to an old fox like him?

963
00:41:26,559 --> 00:41:27,639
Even the King of Hell

964
00:41:27,639 --> 00:41:28,639
would find him too crafty.

965
00:41:28,639 --> 00:41:29,360
He wouldn't even want to take him.

966
00:41:30,599 --> 00:41:31,039
Right?

967
00:41:31,159 --> 00:41:31,679
Old Wei...

968
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,199
It breaks my heart.

969
00:41:35,159 --> 00:41:35,599
Think about it.

970
00:41:36,280 --> 00:41:37,480
I'm like this now,

971
00:41:38,159 --> 00:41:39,239
he's fallen ill too,

972
00:41:39,760 --> 00:41:40,800
and you're leaving.

973
00:41:41,280 --> 00:41:42,280
The three of us old brothers...

974
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:43,760
are we just parting ways like this?

975
00:41:44,719 --> 00:41:47,320
Decades together, just falling apart like this?

976
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:55,360
Brother Wei,

977
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:57,880
Changfu

978
00:41:58,480 --> 00:42:00,000
is your life's work!

979
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:01,400
Sure,

980
00:42:02,719 --> 00:42:04,039
Shi Yongnian

981
00:42:04,519 --> 00:42:05,960
is a big boss now.

982
00:42:06,559 --> 00:42:08,000
But the three of us,

983
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:09,239
after all these years,

984
00:42:09,480 --> 00:42:10,719
through thick and thin,

985
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:12,440
what hurdles haven't we cleared?

986
00:42:12,679 --> 00:42:14,840
Just because he threw a few threats at you,

987
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:15,760
you...

988
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:17,559
you're just going to give up?

989
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:19,079
Xizi is right.

990
00:42:19,320 --> 00:42:20,039
Back in the day,

991
00:42:21,079 --> 00:42:23,079
when we first started this business,

992
00:42:23,639 --> 00:42:25,159
you were a commander with no troops!

993
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:26,599
It was me and Xizi

994
00:42:26,800 --> 00:42:28,840
who followed you through thick and thin,

995
00:42:28,960 --> 00:42:30,199
building the Changfu name

996
00:42:30,280 --> 00:42:32,000
out of the mud and dirt!

997
00:42:32,239 --> 00:42:33,239
N-Now you want to

998
00:42:33,559 --> 00:42:35,119
t-t-toss the two of us aside,

999
00:42:35,280 --> 00:42:36,079
sell out for a big sum,

1000
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:37,880
and just leave us high and dry?!

1001
00:42:38,199 --> 00:42:38,920
I'm telling you,

1002
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:39,679
we're not selling!

1003
00:42:40,239 --> 00:42:41,639
Sell to anyone else, but I'll never sell to him!

1004
00:42:42,280 --> 00:42:43,119
Dacheng, Dacheng!

1005
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:44,679
Calm down! Take it easy!

1006
00:42:44,679 --> 00:42:46,280
You just got out of the hospital, you can't get worked up.

1007
00:42:46,679 --> 00:42:47,280
Besides,

1008
00:42:47,679 --> 00:42:50,119
Brother Wei didn't mean it that way.

1009
00:42:50,440 --> 00:42:50,960
Right?

1010
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:54,360
Still, Brother Wei,

1011
00:42:55,599 --> 00:42:56,599
truth be told,

1012
00:42:57,360 --> 00:43:00,039
if he can take over your company today

1013
00:43:00,039 --> 00:43:01,000
and tear down your sign,

1014
00:43:01,239 --> 00:43:01,840
tomorrow,

1015
00:43:02,400 --> 00:43:04,079
he could destroy our livelihood!

1016
00:43:05,159 --> 00:43:06,960
You buy a plane ticket and fly off,

1017
00:43:07,400 --> 00:43:09,920
throwing the two of us straight into the fire!

1018
00:43:20,079 --> 00:43:21,400
Unite the three into one,

1019
00:43:21,719 --> 00:43:22,880
pull together as one,

1020
00:43:23,199 --> 00:43:24,400
and no one will be able to tear us apart.

1021
00:43:25,480 --> 00:43:26,559
Are you saying...

1022
00:43:28,400 --> 00:43:28,960
a merger?

1023
00:43:29,199 --> 00:43:31,599
You look down on our family's bricklaying business,

1024
00:43:31,599 --> 00:43:32,000
don't you?

1025
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:32,360
No, Dad.

1026
00:43:32,440 --> 00:43:33,440
It's not about looking down on it.

1027
00:43:33,440 --> 00:43:35,199
I've already quit my job.

1028
00:43:35,320 --> 00:43:36,880
I've already started my own law firm.

1029
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:38,360
You insist on dragging me back—

1030
00:43:38,360 --> 00:43:39,320
what for?

1031
00:43:39,519 --> 00:43:41,159
Have you ever considered what I want?

1032
00:43:41,199 --> 00:43:43,239
Aren't you just trying to force my hand?

1033
00:43:43,239 --> 00:43:44,079
You're right.

1034
00:43:44,079 --> 00:43:45,199
I am forcing your hand.

1035
00:43:45,199 --> 00:43:45,719
So what?
